# DSP Platform — Architecture & Trust Governance

## Authoritative docs (do not redesign)

Follow **exactly**:

- PR1.0 Product Strategy & Compliance (`docs/PRODUCT_*`, `RESEARCH_MODE`, `FEATURE_FLAG_*`, `COMPLIANCE_*`)
- PR1.1 Product Experience Blueprint (`docs/PRODUCT_EXPERIENCE_BLUEPRINT.md` and linked PXB docs)
- PR1.2 Visual Language & Interaction System (`docs/PR1_2_*`, `VISUAL_LANGUAGE.md`, etc.)
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md`
- `docs/USER_TRUST_STANDARD.md`
- `docs/PRODUCT_CONSTITUTION.md`
- `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_QUALITY_GATE.md`

If implementation reveals an architectural issue: **STOP**, document the gap, **do not** redesign the platform.

## Thin client

No valuation, recommendation, or AI reasoning in the browser. Use frozen `/api/v1` only. No engine/API/compliance redesign under UI epics.

## User Trust Standard (every insight)

1. **Traceable** — show source (statements, calculated, valuation, AI, consensus, user input)
2. **Explainable** — What / Why / Why care / What next
3. **Consistent** — terminology, ratings, colors, order, VLIS
4. **Actionable** — always a next investigation step
5. **Honest** — category: Verified / Calculated / Estimated / AI / Consensus / User / Unknown / Unavailable; never fabricate
6. **Transparent AI** — separate raw data, calculated metrics, AI interpretation, street opinion
7. **Research first** — educate before recommending; Research Mode labels unless SEBI flags unlock

## Product Constitution (priority order)

Trust → Correctness → Explainability → Consistency → Accessibility → Performance → Visual Polish → Feature Completeness

Never ship polish that reduces trust. Prefer simpler trust-increasing UX.

## Quality gate before COMPLETE

PR1.0–PR1.2 · Governance · Trust · Constitution · Four Questions · Research Mode · Feature flags · A11y · Performance · Responsive · Mobile · Thin client · Regression GREEN

## Implementation return format

Architecture Impact · Components Added · Pages Updated · Feature Flags Used · Accessibility Validation · Performance Validation · Responsive Validation · Known Limitations · Future Enhancements · Regression Summary
